        "conversion_check": {
          "description": "For encoded demonstrated targets, decode reconstructs the FK-commanded world TCP pose from the same causal reference, then shared IK is compared by maximum world position error in metres, rotation angle in radians, and gripper scalar error. Rotation is the continuous 6D projection; IK may choose a nonunique joint solution. The 0.01 bound accommodates independent IK while its nominal solver tolerances remain 1e-4 m and 1e-3 rad.",
