          "tcp_pose"
        ],
        "output_semantics": "Each prediction slot contains [dx,dy,dz,r1x,r1y,r1z,r2x,r2y,r2z,g]. Position is metres relative to a causal smooth reference: a soft nearest-anchor blend of current object position and a drawer-handle anchor target_pose.xyz+[-0.270,0,0.065] m. The weight is sigmoid((distance(TCP,drawer_anchor)-distance(TCP,object))/0.040 m). The six rotation values are the first two columns of an absolute world-frame TCP rotation and are projected by Gram-Schmidt; g is the demonstrated native gripper scalar (nonnegative opens, negative closes). Slot 0 denotes t-1 and slots 1..8 denote executable targets t..t+7. At every executed slot, decode recomputes the reference from the fresh observation, adds the learned offset, projects rotation, and calls panda_kinematics.solve_ik from freshly measured joints. No Cartesian clipping or scripted completion is applied.",
        "parameter_semantics": "No caller parameters are accepted: the sole binding call_args={} means execute the complete retrieve-store-close behavior. All intent is fixed by the task; observed object_pose and target_pose are world-frame metre/wxyz poses, and the policy resolves them causally at every chunk and decode.",
